  "commit_message": "Fix IndexOutOfRangeException on closed generic struct from referenced assembly\n\nMsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer and MessagePackGenerator both crash with an\nIndexOutOfRangeException when a [MessagePackObject] type has a member whose\ntype is a closed generic value type (e.g. a generic record struct) declared\nin a referenced assembly. Because the generator swallows the exception and\nonly emits a CS8785 warning, the affected assembly silently ends up with no\ngenerated resolver at all, which surfaces later as a runtime crash in\ntrimmed/NativeAOT deployments.\n\nThe type/member symbols involved are metadata symbols (no syntax in the\ncurrent compilation), so DeclaringSyntaxReferences is empty. TypeCollector\nindexed DeclaringSyntaxReferences[0] directly at three call sites instead of\nusing FirstOrDefault(), unlike the null-safe pattern already used by\nGetIdentifierLocation/GetLocation/GetParameterListLocation and by the\nequivalent property-loop diagnostic just above one of them. Apply the same\nnull-safe pattern at all three sites so a missing declaration location just\nfalls back to Location.None instead of crashing.\n\nFixes #2283",
  "author": "Akash Kumar",
  "agent_written": false,
